g":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Historic_Bridgetown_and_its_Garrison-115165.jpg/960px-Historic_Bridgetown_and_its_Garrison-115165.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Queen's Park, Bridgetown (Barbados)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":13.0983,"lo":-59.6091,"d":2486,"ds":"Queen's Park is a national park in Barbados. The park was the former home of the Commander of the British Troops stationed in Barbados for the West Indies. Situated in the northeastern segment of the capital city Bridgetown, the park's borders are roughly Roebuck and Crumpton Streets to the north and west, and Halls and Constitution Roads located east and south.","wpu":"Queen's Park, Bridgetown (Barbados)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Queen%27s_Park%2C_Bridgetown_%28Barbados%29.jpg/960px-Queen%27s_Park%2C_Bridgetown_%28Barbados%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Diocese of Bridgetown","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":13.0918,"lo":-59.6089,"d":2807,"ds":"The Diocese of Bridgetown (Latin: Dioecesis Pontipolitana) is a diocese of the Latin Church of the Catholic Church in the Caribbean. The diocese encompasses the entirety of the former British dependency of Barbados. The diocese is a suffragan of the Archdiocese of Port of Spain, and a member of the Antilles Episcopal Conference.","wpu":"Diocese of Bridgetown","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Karte_Kirchenprovinzen_und_Di%C3%B6zesen_der_Karibik.png/960px-Karte_Kirchenprovinzen_und_Di%C3%B6zesen_der_Karibik.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Carlisle Bay, Barbados","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":13.083333,"lo":-59.616667,"d":2866,"ds":"Carlisle Bay is a small natural harbour located in the southwest region of Barbados. The island nation's capital, Bridgetown, is situated on this bay which has been turned into a marine park. Carlisle Bay's marine park is a popular spot on the island for scuba diving.","wpu":"Carlisle Bay, Barbados","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Carlisle_Bay%2C_Barbados.jpg/960px-Carlisle_Bay%2C_Barbados.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Cave Hill, Saint Michael, Barbados","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":13.134013,"lo":-59.630088,"d":3227,"ds":"Cave Hill, St. Michael, is a suburban area situated in the parish of Saint Michael, Barbados. It is located about 4 km north-west of the capital city Bridgetown, along the west coast of Barbados.","wpu":"Cave Hill, Saint Michael, Barbados","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3f/Sign_for_the_University_of_the_West_Indies%2C_Barbados.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Charles Fort (Barbados)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":13.0789,"lo":-59.6127,"d":3514,"ds":"Charles Fort, originally Needham's Fort, is a historic military fortification and UNESCO World Heritage Site in Bridgetown, Barbados. It was originally built in 1650, and rebuilt in 1811. It is located at Needham's Point on the southwestern side of the island, overlooking Carlisle Bay.","wpu":"Charles Fort (Barbados)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Charles_Fort_%2833729930758%29.jpg/960px-Charles_Fort_%2833729930758%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Needham's Point Lighthouse","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":13.078611,"lo":-59.610944,"d":3650,"ds":"Needham's Point Lighthouse is a lighthouse located in the southwest coast of Barbados. Needham's Point lighthouse is one of four still existent historic lighthouses in Barbados. Unlike the others it has a stationary rather than rotating beacon.","wpu":"Needham's Point Lighthouse","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Needhams_Point_Lighthouse%2C_Carlisle_Bay%2C_Barbados_2013-08-04_17-57.jpg/960px-Needhams_Point_Lighthouse%2C_Carlisle_Bay%2C_Barbados_2013-08-04_17-57.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Saint Ann's Fort","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":13.0787,"lo":-59.607,"d":3912,"ds":"Saint Ann's Fort is a historic military fort in Barbados. It is located in the Garrison Historic Area (also known as St. Ann's Garrison or, more commonly, The Garrison).","wpu":"Saint Ann's Fort","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5c/BB_Garrison_Area_1010_%287%29_%2817186832176%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Barbados Museum & Historical Society","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":13.082222,"lo":-59.6025,"d":3992,"ds":"The Barbados Museum & Historical Society is a private organization with public collections. Established in 1933 in the old Military Prison at the Saint Ann's historic Garrison, the museum has more than 500,000 artifacts that depict the island's rich history and natural history. Inclusive of some of these artifacts are antique maps of the island and paintings.","wpu":"Barbados Museum & Historical Society","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Historic_Bridgetown_and_its_Garrison-115163.jpg/960px-Historic_Bridgetown_and_its_Garrison-115163.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Hastings, Barbados","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":13.075556,"lo":-59.597222,"d":4909,"ds":"Hastings is a small village and beach resort in the parish of Christ Church, Barbados on the island's south-western coast. It has beautiful white sandy beaches and is often a location for surfing on the island. Barbados' longest boardwalk, Richard Haynes Boardwalk currently starts from here, and runs Eastward to the nearby community of Rockley.","wpu":"Hastings, Barbados","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Hastings_Beach_-Feb.2026.jpg/960px-Hastings_Beach_-Feb.2026.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Lloyd Erskine Sandiford Centre","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":13.104,"lo":-59.583,"d":5199,"ds":"The Lloyd Erskine Sandiford Centre (formerly known as the Sherbourne Conference Centre) is a conference centre facility on the Caribbean island of Barbados. Owned by the government of Barbados and managed by the government agency Barbados Conference Services Limited (BCSL), the Lloyd Erskine Sandiford Centre is just outside the capital city of Bridgetown, in St. Michael.","wpu":"Lloyd Erskine Sandiford Centre","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/26/Lloyd_Erskine_Sandiford_Conference_And_Cultural_Centre%2C_Barbados-001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Emancipation Statue","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":13.105033,"lo":-59.580089,"d":5513,"ds":"The Emancipation Statue is a public sculpture symbolising the \"breaking of the chains\" of slavery at Emancipation. It is located in Barbados, east of Bridgetown at centre of the J.T.C. Ramsay roundabout formed at the junction of the ABC Highway and Highway 5.","wpu":"Emancipation Statue","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a6/Bussa_statue.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Blue Waters, Barbados","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":13.066667,"lo":-59.583333,"d":6694,"ds":"Blue Waters is a populated place in the parish of Christ Church, Barbados. It is a coastal area located on the south coast of Barbados. Rockley Beach is a beach located in Blue Waters.","wpu":"Blue Waters, Barbados","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Blue_Waters%2C_Barbados.jpg/960px-Blue_Waters%2C_Barbados.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Graeme Hall Nature Sanctuary","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":13.071944,"lo":-59.577778,"d":6836,"ds":"Graeme Hall Nature Sanctuary occupies 42 per cent of the Ramsar wetland at Graeme Hall, in Christ Church, Barbados. It is currently managed by the Barbados Wetlands Trust and the Protector of the Trust is Anthony Da Silva. The Trust was formed by Da Silva in late 2024 and the property was purchased in December 2024.","wpu":"Graeme Hall Nature Sanctuary","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Graeme_Hall_Sanctuary_-_Entrance.jpg/960px-Graeme_Hall_Sanctuary_-_Entrance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Paynes Bay, Barbados","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":13.166667,"lo":-59.633333,"d":6861,"ds":"Paynes Bay, sometimes called the \"Platinum Coast\", is located on the west coast of Barbados. The resort hotel Sandy Lane is situated at the northern end of Paynes Bay.","wpu":"Paynes Bay, Barbados","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Paynes_Bay_view.jpg/960px-Paynes_Bay_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Bridgetown (UN/LOCODE: BB BGI) is the capital and largest city of Barbados. Formerly The Town of Saint Michael, the Greater Bridgetown area is located within the parish of Saint Michael. Bridgetown is sometimes locally referred to as \"The City\", but the most common reference is simply \"Town\".","wpu":"Bridgetown","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Bridgetown_aerial.JPG/960px-Bridgetown_aerial.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}